{"code":"ER_DUP_ENTRY","errno":1062,"index":0,"level":"error","sql":"INSERT INTO scanReport(patientid,billingid,scan,content,sonographer,testid) VALUES ('1706643725522','380','abdominal ultrasound scan','<p>Job Title: Full Stack Web Developer Tier 2 Job Posting Intro: Devops Africa is actively seeking a skilled and motivated Full Stack Web Developer Tier 2 to join our team. As a Full Stack Dev, you will have the opportunity to build and improve web applications in our open source technology environment. Join our collaborative team of professionals and play a vital role in delivering innovative solutions that align with our business objectives. Job Summary: The Full Stack Web Developer Tier 2 is responsible for building new and improving existing web applications in our open source technology environment. This role will create and/or revise applications based off of prioritized business outcomes as well as provide application technical support. This position is remote work eligible. Responsibilities: ● Develop and enhance web applications in an open source technology environment, aligning with prioritized business outcomes.&nbsp;</p><p>● Create and revise applications based on requirements, ensuring adherence to design and architectural principles. ● Provide technical support for applications, troubleshooting issues, and implementing solutions. ● Utilize JavaScript/TypeScript, ReactJS, Node.js, ExpressJS, and REST APIs to build efficient and scalable web applications. ● Work with standard development tools such as Git and Jira for version control, issue tracking, and project management. ● Implement queuing and caching mechanisms using RabbitMQ, Elasticsearch, and Redis for efficient data processing and storage. ● Apply SQL and database design skills, particularly with MySQL/MariaDB, to ensure efficient data storage and retrieval. ● Understand and apply service/worker design patterns to build robust and scalable applications. ● Familiarity with product architecture to ensure development aligns with overall system design. ● Collaborate with the team to work within an existing codebase, maintaining the current design structure and ensuring code quality. ● Follow Scrum principles, understanding the impact of each sprint on the overall project/product. ● Approach problem-solving with agile principles, adapting to changing requirements and priorities. ● Support the team and business in creating small, releasable sprints, delivering value incrementally. ● Champion inspection to assess the project/product direction and identify areas for improvement. ● Actively engage in the Scrum process, identifying and resolving impediments to help the team achieve their goals. ● Participate in company, department, and process changes, actively contributing to their execution and success. ● Facilitate knowledge sharing within the team and seek opportunities for individual and team improvement. ● Train and mentor team members, sharing expertise and fostering professional growth. ● wwInfluence others through the organization\\'s core values, promoting a positive and collaborative work environment. ● Possess and seek understanding of business processes, aligning development efforts with organizational goals. ● Recognize how the team\\'s work impacts other areas within the organization, fostering collaboration and alignment. ● Undertake additional assigned duties as requested Supervisory Responsibilities: ● None Qualifications: ● Bachelor\\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent work experience). ● 5 years of experience ● Strong technical proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, ReactJS, Node.js, ExpressJS, and REST APIs. ● Experience with standard development tools such as Git for version control and Jira for issue tracking. ● Knowledge and practical experience with queuing/caching technologies like RabbitMQ, Elasticsearch, and Redis. ● Proficiency in SQL and database design, particularly with MySQL/MariaDB. ● Familiarity with service/worker design patterns for building scalable and efficient applications. ● Understanding of product architecture and ability to work within an existing codebase while maintaining design structure. ● Thorough understanding of Scrum principles and agile methodologies, including sprint planning and prioritization. ● Proactive involvement in the Scrum process, identifying and resolving impediments to support the team\\'s goals. ● Strong team dynamics, actively participating in company, department, and process changes. ● Demonstrated ability to facilitate knowledge sharing and contribute to team improvement. ● Experience training and mentoring team members, promoting professional growth and development. ● Ability to influence others through the organization\\'s core values, fostering a positive work culture. ● Deep understanding of business processes and the ability to align development efforts with organizational goals. ● Awareness of how the team\\'s work impacts other areas within the organization, promoting collaboration and alignment. ● Ability to adapt to changes in company, department, and process, embracing a growth mindset and a willingness to learn new technologies and practices. ● Excellent team dynamics, including the ability to work collaboratively in a selforganizing Scrum team structure. ● Effective communication skills and the ability to provide and receive feedback constructively. ● A genuine interest in understanding the business processes and needs that the product addresses, ensuring development efforts align with the overall goals. ● Strong problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and a commitment to writing clean, maintainable, and efficient code. Working Settings: ● Full-time Salaried Exempt, not eligible for overtime ● Office hours are 10am-7pm, Monday through Friday, GMT, additional hours may be required depending on priorities ● This position is a full-time work. Compensation: ● The salary is negotiable and varies 